CORE
main_multi.c
--all-properties --solver-time-limit 60
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a is not 1: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ a is not 2: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ holds: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 2 of 3 failed \(3 iterations\)$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
Exercises --solver-time-limit on the multi-property path, which makes several
solver calls on the same solver instance: one for each failing property, plus
a final one. A time limit that is not reached must not affect any of them.
